//! Browser-executed BabyBear proof placement checkpoint.
//!
//! The compute pass derives a four-row Q12 Mandelbrot witness through the
//! production proof kernel, interprets one Conal factor vocabulary as four
//! staged 4-to-16 BabyBear coset LDEs, and commits the resulting 64 field values
//! with the production Poseidon2 sponge. One Fe-authored round interpreter
//! then places the complete `16 -> 8 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1` FRI schedule. Each round
//! derives its own transcript challenge, folds independent pairs, commits the
//! resulting quartic evaluations, reduces their exact ordered Merkle tree,
//! and binds the layer root into the next transcript. The semantic schedule,
//! round domains, pair operation, and Poseidon operations are shared with the
//! scalar proof. Thin actor passes specialize only physical round capacities.
//! Per-invocation progress cursors make repeated dispatch race-free without a
//! host-owned dispatch index. A Fe-authored mutation changes one round-one
//! evaluation after the clean root is fixed; later challenges must diverge
//! only through the authenticated transcript chain. The fragment pass
//! visualizes the retained full fold schedule and status words.
//!
//! This is a mixed placement checkpoint. The four independent LDE columns use
//! the portable stage-grid interpretation of canonical Conal factor trees. The
//! paired commitment and FRI hash states are a second workgroup-map
//! interpretation. Witness generation and final comparison remain scalar
//! passes. This is an exact FRI-subsystem checkpoint whose starting transcript
//! is the clean LDE commitment. It is not yet the full AIR transcript, a
//! shared-memory butterfly interpreter, an authenticated query receipt, or a
//! recursive proof.

